From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not require libutil

libutil is where glibc keeps forkpty(). Windows has no such library, and
nothing in repoeditor calls it -- the terminal is qtermwidget's, with its own
backend. find_library() leaving UTIL_LIBRARY as NOTFOUND then puts the
literal string "UTIL_LIBRARY-NOTFOUND" on the link line, and CMake fails at
generate time before a single object is compiled.

Worth sending upstream: an unfound optional library should not be spliced
into a link line on any platform.
diff --git a/repoeditor/CMakeLists.txt b/repoeditor/CMakeLists.txt
index 6c1dc2b..89d207e 100644
--- a/repoeditor/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/repoeditor/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -5,7 +5,13 @@ else()
 endif()
 
 find_package(Threads REQUIRED)
+# libutil is where glibc keeps forkpty(). Windows has no such library and
+# nothing here calls it: the terminal is qtermwidget's, with its own backend.
+# Not finding it must therefore not be fatal.
 find_library(UTIL_LIBRARY NAMES util)
+if(NOT UTIL_LIBRARY)
+  set(UTIL_LIBRARY "")
+endif()
 
 set(CMAKE_AUTOMOC ON)
 
